490
00:20:14.378 --> 00:20:15.947
 [YELLING & GRUNTING]

491
00:20:17.615 --> 00:20:18.682
 Necklace.

492
00:20:18.683 --> 00:20:20.117
 [SIRENS WAILING]

493
00:20:20.118 --> 00:20:22.319
<i>HUEY:
 As he contemplated spending the remainder</i>

494
00:20:22.320 --> 00:20:24.187
<i>of his natural life in prison,</i>

495
00:20:24.188 --> 00:20:26.356
<i>Granddad never stopped
 to realize</i>

496
00:20:26.357 --> 00:20:28.993
<i>that he had gotten the respect
 he so desperately wanted.</i>

497
00:20:28.994 --> 00:20:32.429
 Yo, that mug killed a blind,
 old man with his bare hands.

498
00:20:32.430 --> 00:20:34.832
 Now, that's gangsta.

499
00:20:34.833 --> 00:20:37.636
 Robert Jebediah Freeman?

500
00:20:39.137 --> 00:20:41.138
<i>Tom and I had gotten
 the fight licensed</i>

501
00:20:41.139 --> 00:20:44.642
<i>by the state boxing commission
 at the last minute,</i>

502
00:20:44.643 --> 00:20:47.911
<i>legally indemnifying Granddad
 against Stinkmeaner's death.</i>

503
00:20:47.912 --> 00:20:51.415
<i>But he was still pretty
 shook up by the whole thing.</i>

504
00:20:51.416 --> 00:20:55.118
<i>Colonel Stinkmeaner had
 no family and no friends.</i>

505
00:20:55.119 --> 00:20:58.422
<i>He lived a life without love
 or companionship,</i>

506
00:20:58.423 --> 00:20:59.656
<i>or even pets.</i>

507
00:20:59.657 --> 00:21:02.426
<i>He was a horrible,
 awful human being.</i>

508
00:21:02.427 --> 00:21:05.262
<i>And in truth, the world
 was better off with him dead.</i>

509
00:21:05.263 --> 00:21:07.298
<i>Still, he was our brother.</i>

510
00:21:07.299 --> 00:21:10.034
 Lord, please forgive us
 for taking this man's life.

511
00:21:10.035 --> 00:21:12.136
 Why you say "us"?
 You killed him...

512
00:21:12.137 --> 00:21:14.371
 Shut your ass and pray, boy.

513
00:21:14.372 --> 00:21:16.374
 [?]

514
00:21:21.213 --> 00:21:23.248
 [?]